<title>GREECE: POSEIDON, ASPIS INCOME LEAD GREEK INCOME FUND RETURNS.</title>
<headline>POSEIDON, ASPIS INCOME LEAD GREEK INCOME FUND RETURNS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poseidon and Aspis Income were</p>
<p>leading 37 Greek fixed income funds in February with</p>
<p>year-to-date returns of 11.7 percent and 5.72 percent</p>
<p>respectively, the association of institutional investors said in</p>
<p>its monthly review.</p>
<p>Assets under management of fixed income funds rose 8.91</p>
<p>percent to 1.66 trillion drachmas at end-February, it said.</p>
<p>	FUND	  ASSETS   CHANGE IN SHARES**   RETURN (YTD)*</p>
<p>		    (drs bln)</p>
<p>1. Poseidon	  1.378	   2.4%		   11.75%</p>
<p>2. Aspis Income   22.640	   5.21%		   5.72%</p>
<p>3. ATE capital     5.383	  42.81%		   5.60%</p>
<p>4. Hermes income  68.874	  -0.34%		   4.59%</p>
<p>5. Metrolife	 1.509	  20.55%		   3.34%</p>
<p>6. Allianz income 12.786	   4.82%		   3.14%</p>
<p>7. Kosmos	   17.14	   13.13%		   2.76%</p>
<p>8. International  13.76	    3.51%		   2.75%</p>
<p>9. Agrotiki	108.37	   -4.49%		   2.52%</p>
<p>10.ETBA Natwest   36.32	    8.95%		   2.44%</p>
<p>11.Hambros	  15.43	    3.76%		   2.43%</p>
<p>12.Delphi income  63.47	    1.20%		   2.36%</p>
<p>13.Ergo income    63.11	    4.63%		   2.35%</p>
<p>14.Helvetia	  3.43	    1.59%		   2.34%</p>
<p>15.Ionian Life     0.78	   -3.27%		   2.33%</p>
<p>16.Interamerican 287.99	    9.38%		   2.26%</p>
<p>income</p>
<p>17.Interamerican   0.34	     ----		   2.26%</p>
<p>long-term</p>
<p>18.Xios income    40.81	   36.24%		   2.15%</p>
<p>19.Midland	  20.71	   16.61%		   2.15%</p>
<p>20.Bank of Athens  4.81	   36.29%		   2.15%</p>
<p>*  Returns are based on NAV on February 28</p>
<p>** It measures inflows/redemptions in February</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
